  "summary": "A Georgetown, Indiana police officer, Justin Craig, was arrested on fraud and official misconduct charges after an internal audit and Indiana State Police investigation found he conducted hundreds of Flock ALPR searches on vehicles belonging to his wife and a previous acquaintance of hers, with no connection to active investigations. He was placed on leave in August 2026 and arrested October 22, 2026; his attorney says the conduct violates no law or policy and plans a motion to dismiss.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "officer Justin Craig conducted numerous searches in 2026 that \"did not appear connected to any authorized investigation.\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "an ISP trooper found 88 searches for the car Craig's wife drives. He also said he found more than 230 searches for a car and motorcycle owned by a \"previous acquaintance\" of hers.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "ISP determined Craig accessed Flock information \"in a manner inconsistent with department policy and without lawful purpose.\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "The conduct alleged does not violate any law or department policy. If the public or police agencies believe it should, the answer is to write that law or policy.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
  ],
